# Owned per-tile reconstruction buffers — measurement record

Branch `perf/tile-owned-recon`, base `main` @ `ee07b00`. Issue #455, Variant 1.
Design + declines + gate list: `docs/TILE_OWNED_RECON.md`.

Host: Apple M4 Pro (12 cores), macOS 26.5.2, aarch64. rustc stable, default
features, **no `-C target-cpu=native`**. dav1d 1.5.4 from Homebrew.

Arms, all four interleaved in ONE sweep with a rotating order:

| arm | build | switch |
|---|---|---|
| `base` | default features | — |
| `tkoff` | `--features tile-owned-recon` | `RAV1D_TILE_OWNED=0` |
| `tkon` | `--features tile-owned-recon` | (default on) |
| `dav1d_fd1` | dav1d 1.5.4 | `--threads t --framedelay 1` |

`tkoff` and `tkon` are **the same binary**, so a `tkon`-vs-`tkoff` delta cannot
be a codegen artifact, and `tkoff`-vs-`base` prices the carrier (the extra
field, the `recon_planes` branch, the per-instance predicate) on its own.

---

## 1. Mechanism — the change is LIVE, and by how much

`--features tile-owned-recon,probe-count`, `probe_tracker <vec> <t> 2`, adds per
frame. This is the check that a silent null cannot survive (#473 shipped an arm
that decoded correctly and measured identically because a `cfg` named the wrong
crate's feature; the registration count was what exposed it).

| vector | t | RAV1D_TILE_OWNED=0 | =1 | delta |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| v4k_8tile | 1 | 7,924,706 | 7,924,706 | 0.0% |
| v4k_8tile | 2 | 22,700,725 | 13,372,343 | **−41.1%** |
| v4k_8tile | 4 | 22,700,725 | 13,372,343 | **−41.1%** |
| v4k_8tile | 8 | 22,700,725 | 13,372,343 | **−41.1%** |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 1 | 10,853,960 | 10,853,960 | 0.0% |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 2 | 21,119,397 | 16,665,593 | **−21.1%** |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 4 | 21,119,397 | 16,665,593 | **−21.1%** |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 8 | 21,119,397 | 16,665,593 | **−21.1%** |

The t=1 rows are identical **by construction** — `setup` declines below two
workers — not by luck. The base 8bpc figures reproduce #455's census
(7,924,706 / 22,700,725) to the byte.

What the residual is: at 8bpc t=8, 13,372,343 − 7,924,706 = 5,447,637
registrations/frame still take the per-row split. That is the **filter chain**,
which is untouched here by design. #455's site census puts the filter chain at
6,389,542/frame, so essentially all of reconstruction's `t>1` excess is gone and
essentially all of the filter chain's remains.

10bpc moves less because less of its registration population is reconstruction.

## 2. Output identity

md5 over every plane's visible pixels, `bench_ab_decode`:

* v4k_8tile 8bpc `a00c11f454328023c58af14d55544cff` — base == tkon == tkoff at
  t = 1, 2, 4, 8.
* v4k_8tile_10b `4f218411bc6ee4cc9c630fe827337fa2` — base == tkon at
  t = 1, 2, 4, 8, 16.

Corpus, `md5_inventory`, set-diffed BY NAME with the actual md5 as the value
(`scripts/perf/md5_setdiff.py`):

| comparison | entries | PASS | differing |
|---|---|---|---|
| committed baseline `aarch64_md5_fixes_2026-08-07_final.tsv.zst` vs head, t=1 | 768 | **766** | **0** |
| base vs head, threaded t=1 | 755 | 753 | **0** |
| base vs head, threaded t=2 | 755 | 753 | **0** |
| base vs head, threaded t=8 | 755 | 753 | **0** |
| head t=1 vs head t=8 | 755 | 753 | **0** |

755 rather than 768 because the two film-grain groups are excluded at t>1 — see
§5.

`cargo test --release --features tile-owned-recon`: `decode_md5_verify` **14/14**,
lib **77/77** (incl. 6 new mechanism tests), `decode_cpu_levels` 6/6,
`decode_md5_committed` 3/3, `cancellation` 6/6.
`multi_decoder_pressure.sh` 12 concurrent decoders x 3 iters x
{1,2,4,8,16} threads on 5 vectors, every md5 matching the serial reference:
**PASS** on the `tkon` arm.

## 3. Peak RSS — a real cost, measured not assumed

`/usr/bin/time -l`, v4k_8tile 8bpc, 20 frames, maximum resident set size:

| arm | t=1 | t=8 |
|---|---|---|
| base | 99.5 MB | 106.3 MB |
| tkon | 99.6 MB | **202.4 MB** (+96.1 MB) |

A tile writes its own columns on every row of its tile row, and a page spans
whole rows, so the resident cost is about `tile_columns x plane_bytes` —
4 x 24.0 MB here. t=1 is flat because the feature declines there.

Two facts this measurement produced:

* **`Vec::try_reserve_exact` + `resize(n, 0)` measured +192.5 MB** (313.3 MB
  peak) because `resize` memsets, faulting in every page of an allocation whose
  point is that most of it is never touched. `vec![0u8; n]` lowers to
  `alloc_zeroed` and halves it. The allocation site carries a comment saying so.
* **`v4k_8tile` is 4:4:4**, not the 4:2:0 that #473's `tile_stitch_cost.rs`
  assumed: all three planes are 8,355,840 bytes with stride 3840
  (`uv_stride == y_stride` means `ss_hor == 0`). Its frame is 25.1 MB, not
  12.44 MB, so **#473's 0.315 ms/frame stitch price is for a frame half this
  size** and should not be quoted against this vector.

Buffers are cached across frames on `(n_tiles, byte_len, stride)`: one
allocation over a 3-frame run, so the fault-in cost is paid once per sequence.

## 4. Gap to dav1d

n = **9** complete rounds, 288 rows, **`foreign_max = 0` on every committed row**
(4 cells discarded and retried), rotating arm order, two-point wall fit at 2 and
20 frames, dav1d in the same sweep. Raw:
`tile_owned_recon_gap_2026-08-09.tsv`; bands:
`tile_owned_recon_bands_2026-08-09.txt`.

ms/frame, median [min..max]:

| vector | t | base | tkoff | tkon | dav1d_fd1 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| v4k_8tile | 1 | 318.8 [316.3..320.4] | 318.6 | 319.2 [315.7..321.7] | 246.6 |
| v4k_8tile | 2 | 198.4 [197.4..199.8] | 199.7 | **184.9** [184.6..186.0] | 125.2 |
| v4k_8tile | 4 | 106.7 [106.1..107.6] | 107.1 | **96.8** [95.8..98.8] | 65.7 |
| v4k_8tile | 8 | 68.2 [64.1..69.7] | 68.8 | **58.1** [54.2..59.4] | 36.3 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 1 | 359.5 | 359.9 | 359.4 | 251.6 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 2 | 207.2 | 207.1 | **202.3** | 127.6 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 4 | 110.5 | 110.8 | **105.7** | 66.9 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 8 | 71.9 [69.2..74.2] | 73.2 | **65.2** [60.3..66.6] | 37.8 |

`tkon/base` and the ratio to dav1d:

| vector | t | tkon/base | bands | base/dav1d | tkon/dav1d |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| v4k_8tile | 1 | 1.0010 | OVERLAP | 1.293 | 1.295 |
| v4k_8tile | 2 | **0.9322** | disjoint | 1.585 | **1.478** |
| v4k_8tile | 4 | **0.9068** | disjoint | 1.625 | **1.474** |
| v4k_8tile | 8 | **0.8525** | disjoint | 1.876 | **1.599** |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 1 | 0.9998 | OVERLAP | 1.429 | 1.429 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 2 | **0.9764** | disjoint | 1.624 | 1.586 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 4 | **0.9563** | disjoint | 1.652 | 1.580 |
| v4k_8tile_10b | 8 | **0.9065** | disjoint | 1.900 | **1.722** |

Scaling t1 -> t8: 8bpc **4.68x -> 5.49x** (dav1d 6.79x); 10bpc 5.00x -> 5.52x
(6.65x). t4 -> t8 inversion ratio 0.639 -> 0.600 (dav1d 0.553).

### The carrier is free — all eight cells OVERLAP

`tkoff` vs `base`: 0.9991 / 1.0067 / 1.0036 / 1.0090 (8bpc) and 1.0012 / 0.9995
/ 1.0025 / 1.0178 (10bpc), **every band overlapping**. The extra
`Rav1dFrameData` field, the `recon_planes` branch and the per-instance
`needs_row_split` predicate cost nothing measurable at either depth. That is a
difference from #473's tile-key carrier, which measured +1.6-2.1% at 10bpc
t=2/t=4 because it widened `WithOffset` from 16 to 24 bytes in a `Copy` struct
passed by value through every kernel — nothing here is on that path.

### It does NOT meet the ~1.30x bar, and it does NOT beat #469

* **The bar is met at exactly one cell**: 8bpc t=1, at 1.295 — and that cell is
  base's number, because the feature is off there. Every cell the change
  actually touches is 1.47-1.72.
* **#469 (`perf/strided-rect`, the column-sharded tracker) is ahead at every
  t>1.** Its independent verification round reports 8bpc
  1.306 / 1.328 / 1.333 / 1.470 against a comparable base
  (quoted from that record, **not re-measured here**), against this branch's
  1.295 / 1.478 / 1.474 / 1.599.
* **This branch is ahead at t=1**: #469 costs 1.4% there (its own report;
  1.293 -> 1.306), this costs nothing (1.293 -> 1.295, bands overlapping).

The reason is exactly the registration counts, and the arithmetic closes:
#469 removes the per-row split from BOTH reconstruction and the filter chain
(22.70 M -> 7.92 M, −65%), this removes it from reconstruction only
(22.70 M -> 13.37 M, −41%). At the campaign's measured **1.00 ns per removed
registration**, 9.33 M removed predicts ~9.3 ms; measured is 68.2 -> 58.1 =
**10.1 ms**. The rule holds a third time.

**They are complementary, not alternatives.** Private recon buffers make the
filter chain the only remaining split population; #469's rectangle record is
what would shrink that. Neither round measured the composition.

## 5. A pre-existing panic the threaded corpus found

`examples/md5_inventory` gained `--threads`; it had defaulted to 1, which is the
blindness #455's verification round named ("the 766/766 corpus gate is
single-threaded, so it cannot see any tile-threading hazard").

At `--threads 2` or `--threads 8`, **`main`'s DEFAULT build panics** on the first
film-grain vector, `8-bit/film_grain/av1-1-b8-23-film_grain-50`:

```
thread 'main' panicked at src/thread_task.rs:534:56:
called `Option::unwrap()` on a `None` value
```

`ttd.delayed_fg.try_write().unwrap()` in the delayed film-grain path. Reproduced
with no tile-owned code compiled in, at both t=2 and t=8, on `base`. Pre-existing
and unrelated; it is why the threaded corpus rows above cover 755 of 768.

## 6. Not measured

x86_64. Miri. `--features unchecked`. t=16 in the timed grid. Any vector with
loop restoration live (#455 item 4's structural blindness is unchanged — both 4K
gap vectors are intra-only with LR off, so `looprestoration*.rs` registers zero
borrows in this grid while LR is active in 696/768 corpus vectors). Frame
threading (`n_fc > 1`), intrabc frames and c-ffi picture allocators all decline
to the shared picture and were not exercised through this path.
`decode_permutations` and the tail of the test suite after it did not complete —
the run was stopped to free the box for the timed sweep; see §7.
